  "prompt": "Find the common rule that maps an input grid to an output grid, given the examples below. Generate a python script that takes a grid as input and transforms it according to the this rule. Anticipate that this program will be applied to several grids, not only the shown test grid.\n\nYour script must define exactly one callable entrypoint:\ndef solve(grid):\nwhere `grid` is passed as a list of lists of integers (list[list[int]]) and the function returns the transformed grid in the same format.\n\nExample 1:\n\nInput:\n0 0 0 2 0 0 0 0 0 5\n0 0 0 2 0 0 0 0 0 5\n0 0 0 2 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 2 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 2 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 2 0 0 0 0 0 0\n2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2\n0 0 0 2 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 2 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 2 0 0 0 0 0 0\nOutput:\n0 2 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 2 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 2 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 2 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 2 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 2 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 2 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 2 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2\n0 2 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput:\n0 0 0 4 0 0 0 0 0 5\n0 0 0 4 0 0 0 0 0 5\n0 0 0 4 0 0 0 0 0 5\n4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4\n0 0 0 4 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 4 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 4 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 4 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 4 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 4 0 0 0 0 0 0\nOutput:\n4 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n4 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n4 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n4 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n4 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n4 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4\n4 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n4 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n4 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n\nExample 3:\n\nInput:\n0 0 0 0 0 0 6 0 0 5\n0 0 0 0 0 0 6 0 0 5\n0 0 0 0 0 0 6 0 0 5\n0 0 0 0 0 0 6 0 0 0\n6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6\n0 0 0 0 0 0 6 0 0 0\n0 0 0 0 0 0 6 0 0 0\n0 0 0 0 0 0 6 0 0 0\n0 0 0 0 0 0 6 0 0 0\n0 0 0 0 0 0 6 0 0 0\nOutput:\n0 0 0 6 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 6 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 6 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 6 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 6 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 6 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 6 0 0 0 0 0 0\n6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6\n0 0 0 6 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 6 0 0 0 0 0 0\n\nExample 4:\n\nInput:\n0 0 0 0 3 0 0 0 0 5\n0 0 0 0 3 0 0 0 0 0\n3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3\n0 0 0 0 3 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 0 3 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 0 3 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 0 3 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 0 3 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 0 3 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 0 3 0 0 0 0 0\nOutput:\n0 0 0 3 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 3 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 3 0 0 0 0 0 0\n3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3\n0 0 0 3 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 3 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 3 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 3 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 3 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 3 0 0 0 0 0 0\n\nBelow is a test input grid.\n\nInput:\n0 0 0 0 0 8 0 0 0 5\n0 0 0 0 0 8 0 0 0 5\n0 0 0 0 0 8 0 0 0 0\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n0 0 0 0 0 8 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 0 0 8 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 0 0 8 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 0 0 8 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 0 0 8 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 0 0 8 0 0 0 0\n\nYour final answer should just be the python script itself, no other text or markdown.",
  "raw_response": "def solve(grid):\n    h = len(grid)\n    w = len(grid[0]) if h else 0\n\n    # Find the special color used for the cross (non-zero, non-5)\n    colors = set()\n    for row in grid:\n        for v in row:\n            if v != 0 and v != 5:\n                colors.add(v)\n    color = next(iter(colors))\n\n    # Count marker cells (5)\n    k = sum(v == 5 for row in grid for v in row)\n\n    # Find the full horizontal and vertical lines of the cross\n    cross_row = None\n    cross_col = None\n\n    for r in range(h):\n        if all(grid[r][c] == color for c in range(w)):\n            cross_row = r\n            break\n\n    for c in range(w):\n        if all(grid[r][c] == color for r in range(h)):\n            cross_col = c\n            break\n\n    # Shift cross: left by k, down by k\n    new_row = cross_row + k\n    new_col = cross_col - k\n\n    # Build output\n    out = [[0 for _ in range(w)] for _ in range(h)]\n\n    if 0 <= new_row < h:\n        for c in range(w):\n            out[new_row][c] = color\n\n    if 0 <= new_col < w:\n        for r in range(h):\n            out[r][new_col] = color\n\n    return out",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    h = len(grid)\n    w = len(grid[0]) if h else 0\n\n    # Find the special color used for the cross (non-zero, non-5)\n    colors = set()\n    for row in grid:\n        for v in row:\n            if v != 0 and v != 5:\n                colors.add(v)\n    color = next(iter(colors))\n\n    # Count marker cells (5)\n    k = sum(v == 5 for row in grid for v in row)\n\n    # Find the full horizontal and vertical lines of the cross\n    cross_row = None\n    cross_col = None\n\n    for r in range(h):\n        if all(grid[r][c] == color for c in range(w)):\n            cross_row = r\n            break\n\n    for c in range(w):\n        if all(grid[r][c] == color for r in range(h)):\n            cross_col = c\n            break\n\n    # Shift cross: left by k, down by k\n    new_row = cross_row + k\n    new_col = cross_col - k\n\n    # Build output\n    out = [[0 for _ in range(w)] for _ in range(h)]\n\n    if 0 <= new_row < h:\n        for c in range(w):\n            out[new_row][c] = color\n\n    if 0 <= new_col < w:\n        for r in range(h):\n            out[r][new_col] = color\n\n    return out",
